{'review': '<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\n{\n  "overall_status": "REJECTED",\n  "quality_score": 3.5,\n  "summary": {\n    "critical": 1,\n    "high": 0,\n    "medium": 3,\n    "low": 0,\n    "passed_checks": [\n      "No hardcoded secrets (aside from the CSRF token placeholder)",\n      "Proper use of AbortController for timeouts",\n      "CSRF token included in state-changing operations",\n      "HTTP status code validation",\n      "Modular code structure"\n    ]\n  },\n  "findings": [\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-001",\n      "severity": "critical",\n      "category": "security",\n      "title": "Hardcoded CSRF token in getCsrfToken function",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [7, 11],\n      "description": "The getCsrfToken function returns a hardcoded dummy CSRF token (\'dummy-csrf-token-for-dev\'). In production, this must be replaced with a securely generated token (e.g., from a cookie or meta tag). Using a fixed token makes CSRF protection ineffective.",\n      "impact": "Attackers can perform CSRF attacks because the token is predictable and constant, allowing them to trick users into performing unwanted actions on the application.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Replace the hardcoded token with a secure retrieval mechanism. For example, read the token from a cookie or a meta tag in the HTML.",\n      "code_before": "const getCsrfToken = (): string => {\\n  // For demonstration, returning a dummy token.\\n  // In production, ensure this is securely generated and retrieved.\\n  return \'dummy-csrf-token-for-dev\';\\n};",\n      "code_after": "const getCsrfToken = (): string => {\\n  // Example: read from a cookie named \'csrf-token\'\\n  const match = document.cookie.match(/csrf-token=([^;]+)/);\\n  return match ? decodeURIComponent(match[1]) : \'\';\\n  // Alternatively, from a meta tag:\\n  // const meta = document.querySelector(\'meta[name=\\"csrf-token\\"]\');\\n  // return meta ? meta.getAttribute(\'content\') : \'\';\\n};",\n      "references": ["OWASP-ASVS v4.0.3: 5.1.1", "CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-002",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing input validation for title in createTodo",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [33, 47],\n      "description": "The createTodo function does not validate the title parameter. It should check for empty string, excessive length, or potentially harmful content before making the request.",\n      "impact": "Invalid or malicious input (e.g., extremely long strings, XSS payloads) could be sent to the API, leading to bad requests, storage issues, or potential injection vulnerabilities if the API does not sanitize input.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add validation for the title parameter (e.g., non-empty, reasonable length) before making the request.",\n      "code_before": "export const createTodo = async (title: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL, {\\n    method: \'POST\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ title }),\\n  });\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to create todo: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n};",\n      "code_after": "export const createTodo = async (title: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  if (!title || title.trim() === \'\') {\\n    throw new Error(\'Title cannot be empty\');\\n  }\\n  if (title.length > 200) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Title is too long (max 200 characters)\');\\n  }\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL, {\\n    method: \'POST\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ title }),\\n  });\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to create todo: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n};",\n      "references": ["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-003",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing input validation for id in completeTodo",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [49, 61],\n      "description": "The completeTodo function does not validate the id parameter. It should check for empty string or invalid format (e.g., UUID, numeric) before making the request.",\n      "impact": "An invalid ID (e.g., empty string, malformed UUID) could lead to a bad request or unexpected behavior on the server, potentially causing errors or security issues if the API relies on the ID for authorization checks.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add validation for the id parameter (e.g., non-empty, matches expected format like UUID or numeric).",\n      "code_before": "export const completeTodo = async (id: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(`${API_BASE_URL}/${id}/complete`, {\\n    method: \'PUT\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n  });\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to complete todo: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n};",\n      "code_after": "export const completeTodo = async (id: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  if (!id || id.trim() === \'\') {\\n    throw new Error(\'ID cannot be empty\');\\n  }\\n  // Optional: if ID is expected to be a UUID, validate format\\n  // if (!/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i.test(id)) {\\n  //   throw new Error(\'Invalid ID format\');\\n  // }\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(`${API_BASE_URL}/${id}/complete`, {\\n    method: \'PUT\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n  });\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to complete todo: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n};",\n      "references": ["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-004",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing error handling for non-JSON responses",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [25, 30, 33, 46, 49, 60],\n      "description": "The functions getTodos, createTodo, and completeTodo call response.json() without handling the case where the response is not valid JSON. This can lead to unhandled promise rejections if the API returns a non-JSON response (e.g., HTML error page).",\n      "impact": "If the API returns a non-JSON response, the application will throw an error that is not caught by the function, potentially causing the UI to crash or show an unhelpful error message to the user.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Wrap the response.json() call in a try-catch block and throw a more descriptive error if JSON parsing fails.",\n      "code_before": "export const getTodos = async (): Promise<Todo[]> => {\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL);\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch todos: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n};",\n      "code_after": "export const getTodos = async (): Promise<Todo[]> => {\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL);\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch todos: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  try {\\n    return await response.json();\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Failed to parse JSON response from server\');\\n  }\\n};",\n      "references": []\n    }\n  ],\n  "positive_observations": [\n    "The fetchWithTimeout function correctly uses AbortController to implement request timeouts, preventing hanging requests.",\n    "State-changing operations (createTodo, completeTodo) include the CSRF token in the request header, which helps prevent CSRF attacks when a proper token is used.",\n    "The code checks HTTP response status via response.ok and throws descriptive errors for non-successful responses.",\n    "The code is modular, with clear separation of concerns, and uses TypeScript for type safety."\n  ]\n}\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>'}